    {
      "id": "Lax345332.ThreeFourSat",
      "path": "concepts/Lax345332/ThreeFourSat.lean",
      "title": "(3,4)-satisfiability is NP-hard",
      "type": "theorem",
      "description": "*(3,4)-SAT* is satisfiability restricted to formulas in which every clause contains\nexactly three literals and every variable occurs at most four times. Tovey proved that it\nis NP-hard: every language in NP has a polynomial-time many-one reduction to it.",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Formalization notes",
          "markdown": "The restriction is a predicate on the CNF formulas of the archive's Cook–Levin submission,\nso the encoding and the notion of satisfiability are shared with unrestricted SAT.\nOccurrences are counted with multiplicity."
        }
      ],
      "imports": [
